[[File:Map042.png|center|350px]]
'''Konjac Valley''' (イトコンバレー, ''Itokon Barē'', '''ITcon Valley''') is the 11th sub-chapter of [[Zero Legends]], and the 109th sub-chapter overall. It was introduced in [[Version 13.3 Update|Version 13.3]] and is available up to {{2c}} difficulty.

==Difficulty==
This sub-chapter, similarly to the [[Stratospheric Pathway|previous one]] is not that difficult. You might have trouble with the [[Metallic Metaverse|third stage]], but besides that, every stage here should only take an attempt or two. There is a focus in this sub-chapter on [[Metal Enemies]], with every odd numbered stage having at least one, so if they aren't your things, you may not have fun here.
{{LegendDiff|120}}

==New Features==
This sub-chapter introduces 3 enemies to Zero Legends:
*[[Dark Dober]]: A [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]]/[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] variant of [[Dober P.D]] that has very high health, much higher speed, a guaranteed chance to weaken cats to 25%, a 1 in 3 chance for a Lv.3 [[Mini-Wave]] and an Omni Strike that extends up to 350 range, but is easily knocked back.
*[[Pure Gold R.Ost]]: A [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] variant of [[R.Ost]] from [[GOLD RUSH#The Midas Touch|The Midas Touch]]. Much weaker overall, with no [[Critical Hit|Criticals]] and only 60 HP at the 300% buff it appears with in this sub-chapter, but still has 260 range.
*[[Metal Cyclone]]: A Metal [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]] from [[Attack on Titanium (Insane)|Sweet Irony]]. With lethal damage and incredibly high health for a Metal enemy, its main weaknesses are its low range and speed and high knockback count.

