==Trivia==
*Konjac Valley's Japanese name, Itokon Valley, is a reference to the technology hub [[wikipedia:Silicon Valley|Silicon Valley]], hence why [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal Enemies]] appear in all the odd-numbered stages. Silicon Valley is located in Northern California, thus continuing the American theme that began in [[Stratospheric Pathway]].
**"Itokon" may come from a conversion of "IT" (Information Technology) into Japanese, fitting with the theme of the sub-chapter. It may also be derived from 糸 ''ito'' (thread, yarn or string) or 従兄弟 ''itoko'' (cousin).
*All stages' Japanese names appear to reference companies or the Internet:
**[[Meandering Road|Revolving Expressway]] may refer to the Internet being a technological revolution and an information superhighway linking the globe.
***Note that this name is a translation of ぐるぐる自動車道 Guruguru Jidōshadō, where ぐるぐる ''guruguru'' (onomatopoeia for revolving) sounds similar to グーグル ''Gūguru'' ([[wikipedia:Google|Google]]) and 自動車道 ''jidōshadō'' (expressway) contains the word 自動車 ''jidōsha'' (car), therefore it could also be referencing the [[wikipedia:Google Self-Driving Car Project|Google Self-Driving Car Project]] or [[wikipedia:Google Drive|Google Drive]].
**[[One-Second Photo|Instant Photographic Studio]] may refer to the photo sharing platform [[wikipedia:Instagram|Instagram]].
**[[Metallic Metaverse]] mentions the [[wikipedia:Metaverse|metaverse]].
**[[Pineapple Merchant|Pineapple Trading]] may refer to the technology company [[wikipedia:Apple (company)|Apple]].
**[[Groundscraper|Micro Highrise Building]] may refer to the technology company [[wikipedia:Microsoft|Microsoft]].
**[[Phantom Bluebird|Illusion of the Blue Bird]] may refer to the original logo of the social media site [[wikipedia:Twitter|Twitter/X]], a blue bird.
***The [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] and [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemies in this stage and its background (the dark forest from [[Le'Grim Strikes]]) could represent the new logo, a white X against a black background.
*The Metal enemies in all the odd-numbered stages incentivize use of [[Princess Kaguya (Uber Rare Cat)|Princess Kaguya]]'s [[Ultra Form]] and [[Kubiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|E. Kubilan Pasalan]]'s [[Talents]], both of which were added in [[Version 13.3 Update|Version 13.3]] alongside Konjac Valley.

